7D7AF][/dim]Typing `#sase/` in the ACE prompt bar under a `#gh:sase` VCS tag [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]completes the project's local xprompts (`#sase/reads`, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`#sase/sync`), project-local xprompts are namespaced with exactly [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]one user-facing name everywhere, and those references resolve [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]regardless of the process working directory.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_project_identity.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Canonical project-identity resolver[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity: add a single Python helper that normalizes any project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]spelling (directory key, PROJECT_NAME, alias) to the canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]user-facing namespace name, plus its unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Namespace and filter the xprompt catalog by user-facing name[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog: make the xprompt catalog namespace, tag, and filter [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-local xprompts by the canonical user-facing project name so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requesting project `sase` returns `sase/reads`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Resolve registry-backed project xprompts independent of cwd[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolver: teach the xprompt loader to read a registered project's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checkout xprompts through the project registry so `#sase/reads` expands [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]even when the process cwd is not that checkout.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Normalize the ACE completion project boundary[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui: normalize the project identity the ACE prompt bar derives from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]VCS tag and the prompt context, and add the end-to-end regression test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for the reported completion failure.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mirror the identity fix in the Rust core catalog[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_parity: apply the same canonical-name namespacing and filtering to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the Rust xprompt catalog in the sase-core repo so the LSP and gateway [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agree with Python.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ac","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-ac.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-139f93092c5339a51cd2efc158405512","started_at":"2026-07-28T11:42:41.113986+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785243491,"sha":"b449b8a4b5a133ded4771fa07e22307bf97620cb","subject":"fix(xprompt): normalize ACE completion project identity (sase-ac.4)"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"78efa1775ecfdb44c9abcdb893a5ccd5a9234588f20bab594113a72fa131169a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac.4/chat.md","size_bytes":5158},"commits":{"digest":"8b9fc8dc25b3b18df5f5c10cd5ab5a97de56cfa15f7b